# XFlow Main Cursor Rules

You are operating a generic XFlow development repository.

Read these files before acting:

- `SKILL.md`
- `references/issue-template.md`
- `references/xflow-map.md`
- `AGENTS.md` and `README.md` when present

Runtime rules:

- Do not require Codex. Use repository files and `devctl` commands as the
  source of truth.
- Use `devctl` or `devctl.ps1` from the repository root when available.
- Treat `devctl` / `devctl.ps1` as the only supported workflow entrypoints.
  Do not import or call `xflow.providers` directly, and do not call GitHub or
  Gitee APIs outside devctl during normal workflow execution.
- User-level parameters belong in `~/.xflow/env.local`. Legacy
  `~/gitee.env.local` may be read for compatibility. Never print token values.
- Do not put `XFLOW_PLATFORM` in user-level `~/.xflow/env.local` when working
  across both GitHub and Gitee projects. Use project-local
  `.xflow/local/env.local`, explicit `XFLOW_ENV_FILE`, or the process
  environment for platform overrides.
- Use `XFLOW_PLATFORM=github|gitee` only to select devctl's provider. Do not
  call GitHub or Gitee APIs directly from the AI workflow.
- Maintain `.xflow/current-task.md` for active tasks and run
  `devctl check current-task --issue <id>` before local approval, commit,
  push, PR/MR creation, and cleanup.
- Prefer `devctl.ps1` on Windows. Avoid `git ... 2>&1 | Out-String` and other
  native-command pipelines when the exit code matters.
- Prepare remote body files before remote writes:
  - `.xflow/issues/issue-draft/issue-draft.md`
  - `.xflow/issues/issue-<id>/comment-draft.md`
  - `.xflow/issues/issue-<id>/mr-draft.md`
- Run `devctl check issue-draft`, `devctl check mr-draft`, and
  `devctl check local-review` before remote writes.
- Core remote writes are `issue-create`, `issue-comment`, `issue-close`, and
  `git-mr`; they require local human review of the exact file being published
  or used as evidence.
- After PR/MR creation, use `state-update-suggestion.md` only for local state
  updates. Do not create another PR only to commit post-merge state metadata.
- Use the user's language for Git-related public text: commit messages, remote
  Issue text, remote PR/MR text, review comments, and branch task summaries.
  Do not expand this rule to unrelated source code or docs.

Git commit rules:

- Do not add Cursor co-author trailers.
- Do not append `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` to commit
  messages.
- Do not use `git commit --trailer` to add Cursor, cursoragent, or AI-client
  co-author metadata.
- If a repository already contains such a trailer in an old commit, do not
  rewrite history unless the human reviewer explicitly requests it.
- Direct `main` maintenance is an exception only for the `xflow-devctl` and
  `xflow-skills` tool repositories when the user explicitly requests it. Do
  not apply that exception to ordinary user projects.
